  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-49014",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In GDAL 3.1.0 through 3.13.0, scanForGeometryContainers in the netCDF  ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In GDAL 3.1.0 through 3.13.0, scanForGeometryContainers in the netCDF driver allows code execution via a stack-based buffer overflow. It reads a geometry attribute into a fixed-size stack buffer without validating the attribute length. The attacker embeds the exploit as an oversized geometry attribute in a crafted NetCDF file. This achieves arbitrary code execution on the server running GDAL. This is in frmts/netcdf/netcdfsg.cpp."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-49014",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-49014\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: GDAL\nFixed Version: 3.13.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-49014](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-49014)\nIn GDAL 3.1.0 through 3.13.0, scanForGeometryContainers in the netCDF driver allows code execution via a stack-based buffer overflow. It reads a geometry attribute into a fixed-size stack buffer without validating the attribute length. The attacker embeds the exploit as an oversized geometry attribute in a crafted NetCDF file. This achieves arbitrary code execution on the server running GDAL. This is in frmts/netcdf/netcdfsg.cpp.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-49014**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|GDAL|3.13.1|[CVE-2026-49014](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-49014)|\n\nIn GDAL 3.1.0 through 3.13.0, scanForGeometryContainers in the netCDF driver allows code execution via a stack-based buffer overflow. It reads a geometry attribute into a fixed-size stack buffer without validating the attribute length. The attacker embeds the exploit as an oversized geometry attribute in a crafted NetCDF file. This achieves arbitrary code execution on the server running GDAL. This is in frmts/netcdf/netcdfsg.cpp."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.4,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.4",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8087",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A security flaw has been discovered in OSGeo gdal up to 3.13.0dev-4. I ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A security flaw has been discovered in OSGeo gdal up to 3.13.0dev-4. Impacted is the function GDnentries of the file frmts/hdf4/hdf-eos/GDapi.c. Performing a manipulation of the argument DataFieldName results in heap-based buffer overflow. The attack must be initiated from a local position. The exploit has been released to the public and may be used for attacks. Upgrading to version 3.13.0RC1 is recommended to address this issue. The patch is named 184f77dbcc74118c062c05e464c88161d3c37b9b. You should upgrade the affected component."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-8087",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-8087\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: GDAL\nFixed Version: 3.13.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-8087](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-8087)\nA security flaw has been discovered in OSGeo gdal up to 3.13.0dev-4. Impacted is the function GDnentries of the file frmts/hdf4/hdf-eos/GDapi.c. Performing a manipulation of the argument DataFieldName results in heap-based buffer overflow. The attack must be initiated from a local position. The exploit has been released to the public and may be used for attacks. Upgrading to version 3.13.0RC1 is recommended to address this issue. The patch is named 184f77dbcc74118c062c05e464c88161d3c37b9b. You should upgrade the affected component.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-8087**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|GDAL|3.13.0|[CVE-2026-8087](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-8087)|\n\nA security flaw has been discovered in OSGeo gdal up to 3.13.0dev-4. Impacted is the function GDnentries of the file frmts/hdf4/hdf-eos/GDapi.c. Performing a manipulation of the argument DataFieldName results in heap-based buffer overflow. The attack must be initiated from a local position. The exploit has been released to the public and may be used for attacks. Upgrading to version 3.13.0RC1 is recommended to address this issue. The patch is named 184f77dbcc74118c062c05e464c88161d3c37b9b. You should upgrade the affected component."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.3,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L",
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 1.9,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:P",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.3",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8088",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A weakness has been identified in OSGeo gdal up to 3.13.0dev-4. The af ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A weakness has been identified in OSGeo gdal up to 3.13.0dev-4. The affected element is the function GDfieldinfo of the file frmts/hdf4/hdf-eos/GDapi.c. Executing a manipulation can lead to out-of-bounds read. The attack needs to be launched locally. The exploit has been made available to the public and could be used for attacks. Upgrading to version 3.13.0RC1 is sufficient to fix this issue. This patch is called a791f70f8eaec540974ec989ca6fb00266b7646c. The affected component should be upgraded."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-8088",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-8088\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: GDAL\nFixed Version: 3.13.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-8088](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-8088)\nA weakness has been identified in OSGeo gdal up to 3.13.0dev-4. The affected element is the function GDfieldinfo of the file frmts/hdf4/hdf-eos/GDapi.c. Executing a manipulation can lead to out-of-bounds read. The attack needs to be launched locally. The exploit has been made available to the public and could be used for attacks. Upgrading to version 3.13.0RC1 is sufficient to fix this issue. This patch is called a791f70f8eaec540974ec989ca6fb00266b7646c. The affected component should be upgraded.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-8088**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|GDAL|3.13.0|[CVE-2026-8088](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-8088)|\n\nA weakness has been identified in OSGeo gdal up to 3.13.0dev-4. The affected element is the function GDfieldinfo of the file frmts/hdf4/hdf-eos/GDapi.c. Executing a manipulation can lead to out-of-bounds read. The attack needs to be launched locally. The exploit has been made available to the public and could be used for attacks. Upgrading to version 3.13.0RC1 is sufficient to fix this issue. This patch is called a791f70f8eaec540974ec989ca6fb00266b7646c. The affected component should be upgraded."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 3.3,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L",
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 1.9,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:P",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "3.3",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-39824",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Invoking integer overflow in NewNTUnicodeString in golang.org/x/sys/windows"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "NewNTUnicodeString does not check for string length overflow. When provided with a string that overflows the maximum size of a NTUnicodeString (a 16-bit number of bytes), it returns a truncated string rather than an error."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39824",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-39824\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: golang.org/x/sys\nFixed Version: 0.44.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-39824](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39824)\nNewNTUnicodeString does not check for string length overflow. When provided with a string that overflows the maximum size of a NTUnicodeString (a 16-bit number of bytes), it returns a truncated string rather than an error.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-39824**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|golang.org/x/sys|0.44.0|[CVE-2026-39824](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39824)|\n\nNewNTUnicodeString does not check for string length overflow. When provided with a string that overflows the maximum size of a NTUnicodeString (a 16-bit number of bytes), it returns a truncated string rather than an error."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "0.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "UNKNOWN"
                ]
              }
